== Default output modes ==

Libultra and Libdragon software using SDK-provided default VI modes output signals corresponding with these profiles. Refresh rates are derived from the X1 crystal frequency and VI register values.<ref>Full <math>f_V</math> derivations are shown in [https://github.com/meauxdal/N64-Refresh-Rate-Reference N64 Refresh Rate Reference.]</ref>

{| class="wikitable" style="text-align: center;"
! Standard !! Scan type !! Resolution !! Refresh rate (Hz)
|-
| '''NTSC''' || Progressive || 640×240p || 59.8261054535
|-
| '''NTSC''' || Interlaced || 640×480i || 59.9400599401
|-
| '''PAL''' || Progressive || 640×288p || 49.9201282452
|-
| '''PAL''' || Interlaced || 640×576i || 50
|-
| '''MPAL''' || Progressive || 640×240p || 59.8370742270
|-
| '''MPAL''' || Interlaced || 640×480i || 59.9702194092
|}

Libdragon additionally defines PAL60 configurations combining NTSC resolutions and refresh rates with the PAL color subcarrier.
